The TypeScript adaptation rounds to float32 after every operation of the
float kernels, refuses the direct form I transform (di, the default), blocksize,
channel subsets, a0=0, coefficient sets outside the second-order stability
triangle (and, for zdf, an unstable state matrix), coefficients beyond the
float range, non-finite input or output, timeline enable, expressions and
runtime commands instead of approximating them, always writes a new owned
output frame, declares the per-channel cache in reserve(), enforces explicit
allocation limits and AbortSignal, and adds no FFmpeg runtime code.
The original source and full notices remain in the pinned upstream submodule.
